  "codex_feedback_round1": "VERDICT: NEEDS_REVISION\nReason: candidate is not promotable as written because it ends mid-sentence, overstates \u201cno WholeReduce\u201d in tension with P-P47 / ascend950pr.md\u2019s \u201c\u226464 fp32 run one call\u201d heuristic, and mixes dense packed rows with an 8-lane padded final layout. The tiled per-block mask is only correct when each row\u2019s final partials are stored at an 8-fp32 row stride; otherwise it silently skips/reads wrong lanes.\n\nREVISED_TITLE:\nTree-reduce wide fp32 rows with `BlockReduceMax/Sum` partials; use explicit dense vs 8-lane-padded stage layouts\n\nREVISED_BODY:\n`applies_to: op_class=row_reduction (W >= 64 fp32 elements per row, R parallel rows in UB); soc=Ascend910_V220 / Ascend950PR (fp32 BlockReduceMax/BlockReduceSum confirmed public-API); cann=9.0.0+`\n`derived-from: cann-source (FA-class fp32 online-softmax row reductions, 2026-05-10 revise-cl5)`\n`verified_on: cann-source (read-only); unverified_on: a5_ops`\n`local-kb-crossref: P-P47 (half-interval scalar finish), ascend950pr.md WholeReduce/BlockReduce Sort/Reduce VEC primitive specs`\n\n**Trigger**: Need rowmax or rowsum of wide fp32 rows inside a hot kernel loop, with multiple rows resident in UB. Scalar `GetValue` per element is the anti-pattern: it turns row reduction into `R * W` scalar-pipe work.\n\n**Recommendation**:\n\nUse chained `AscendC::BlockReduceMax<float, false>` / `AscendC::BlockReduceSum<float, false>` stages to reduce each 64-fp32 repeat into 8 fp32 partials. Each repeat views the source as eight 32-byte blocks, each block holding 8 fp32 lanes, and emits one partial per block.\n\nThis pattern is for multi-row packed UB reductions where preserving row parallelism matters. It does not replace P-P47 for a single row or for a simple `count <= 64` reduction: ascend950pr.md says `WholeReduce*` and `BlockReduce*` have similar ~100-cycle floor at 64 fp32, so do not claim an automatic primitive-level speedup for the <=64 scalar finish.\n\n**Layout contract**:\n\nThere are two legal stage layouts. Pick one and keep it explicit.\n\n1. **Dense partial layout**: after each stage, row `r` has `ceil(width / 8)` valid partials stored contiguously with row stride exactly that partial count. This minimizes UB, but a final tiled per-8-lane mask is not valid unless the rows are repacked or padded first.\n\n2. **8-lane-padded final layout**: before the final `BlockReduce*`, each row\u2019s `k <= 8` valid partials must occupy lanes `0..k-1` of an 8-fp32 block, with row stride 8. Only in this layout is the tiled mask \u201clow k bits of every byte\u201d correct.\n\n**Mask contract**:\n\n- `<float, false>` means `isSetMask = false`: the instruction uses the externally configured vector mask. It does not mean unmasked.\n- The vector mask gates source lanes that contribute to the reduction. It does not choose which destination lanes are written.\n- Full 64-fp32 repeats: set full mask once and leave it.\n- Dense intermediate stage with row width `m < 64` but `m > 8`: use a contiguous mask of `m` lanes and set source repeat stride to `ceil(m / 8)` blocks.\n- Final padded stage with `k <= 8`: use a tiled per-block mask that enables lanes `0..k-1` in every 8-lane block, then restore full mask before unrelated VEC work.\n- If `R` is not a multiple of 8 for the final padded stage, either pad the final scratch to a whole 64-lane repeat or handle the last partial repeat with a correct mask and ignored extra outputs. Do not read past allocated UB.\n\n**Final tiled mask helper**:\n```cpp\n__aicore__ inline void SetTiledBlockReduceMask(uint32_t lanesPerBlock) {\n    if (lanesPerBlock >= 8) {\n        AscendC::SetVectorMask<int8_t>((uint64_t)-1, (uint64_t)-1);\n        return;\n    }\n    uint64_t sub = ((uint64_t)1 << lanesPerBlock) - 1;\n    uint64_t tiled = (sub << 0) | (sub << 8) | (sub << 16) | (sub << 24)\n                   | (sub << 32) | (sub << 40) | (sub << 48) | (sub << 56);\n    AscendC::SetVectorMask<int8_t>(tiled, tiled);\n}\n```\n\n**Do not apply**:\n\n- Non-fp32 paths: half/bf16 reduction shapes differ.\n- Rows with `W < 64`: use a simple masked reduction.\n- Kernels that need original source data after destructive in-place staging unless source is copied first.\n- Any target where fp32 `BlockReduceMax/Sum` has not been probe-compiled and numerically validated.\n\n**Transfer targets**: FA softmax rowmax/rowsum, LayerNorm row mean/variance, RmsNorm rowsumsq, GroupNorm group stats, and wide vocabulary softmax reductions.",
